        "explanation": "I left this file unchanged. Both diagnostics come from the same comment, `hmr.ts:323` (`// TODO Trigger their dispose callbacks.`), and I couldn't clear them without breaking one of your rules.\n\n- **Doing the TODO changes runtime behavior.** It means making `prunePaths` call each pruned module's `disposeMap` callback before its `pruneMap` callback. That is new behavior, and your rules say to keep runtime behavior the same. Dispose callbacks can return a `Promise`, so doing it properly also means changing `prunePaths` to return `Promise<void>` instead of `void`. Callers in other files would then need updating, and I'm only allowed to edit this one. Later Vite versions made this exact change: an async `prunePaths` that awaits the disposers, then runs the prune callbacks. The file header says this is a copy of Vite's code, so doing it here would also make it drift from that copy.\n- **Rewording or deleting the comment would only hide the gap.** The comment is the only record that pruned modules skip their dispose callbacks. Rewording it to avoid the word \"TODO\" is the kind of restyling your rules exclude, and deleting it would lose that record.\n\nSomeone needs to decide whether to adopt the newer Vite behavior, including the async signature change and the caller updates. Once that's decided, the fix is about 6 lines in `prunePaths`, and the comment can go."
      },
